## 5. Data Quality Flags

| # | Flag | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Canada table fails to query | Cannot assess this market at all until resolved |
| 2 | RSM linkage only present in US | Any RSM-based matching logic will silently return nothing for 22 of 23 queryable tables |
| 3 | `sgmntTypeCde` only populated in Global | Country-table control extraction must use `objRel[CNTRL]`, not the simpler direct-field check |
| 4 | Whitespace-only segment text (5 tables) | Inflates "segments with text" completeness metrics; real content is thinner than reported |
| 5 | 11 of 24 tables have ≤2 policies | Small-sample findings for those markets carry low statistical confidence |
| 6 | 1 Australian policy has no policyText | Will produce an empty embedding for that record unless handled explicitly |

## 6. Questions for Policy SME

### Critical

1. **[Canada]** Query returned `FAILED: Unable to determine type for field 'json_data'` /
   `Must pass schema, or at least one RecordBatch`. Is this table genuinely empty, a permissions
   issue, or does its schema differ from the other country tables?
2. **[Cross-table — all except US]** RSM linkage was found only in the US table (346 segments / 19
   policies via `objRel.plcyObjTypeCde = 'REG'`). Every other table, including Global, shows zero.
   Is RSM tagging a US-specific practice, or is this linkage simply not yet populated for other
   markets?
3. **[Cross-table — Global vs. country tables]** `sgmntTypeCde` carries the L1C control code
   directly only in the Global table. Every country-specific table has it null throughout. Is
   control identification for country tables meant to rely solely on `objRel[CNTRL]`, or should
   `sgmntTypeCde` be populated there too?
4. **[External table]** A colleague shared a separate, already-flattened segment-level table
   (`plcy_core_id`, `sgmnt_type_cde`, `plcy_obj_id` e.g. `RSM-00030304`, `plcy_obj_type_cde = 'REG'`,
   `cntl_id`, `risk_txnmy_l1/l2/l3_text`). Is this the authoritative curated table we should join
   against instead of parsing RSM/control linkage out of the raw JSON ourselves?

### Standard

5. **[Brazil, China, Taiwan, Hong Kong, Indonesia]** Segment-text median of ~1 character despite
   "100% segments with text" — likely whitespace-only placeholders. Expected for these markets, or
   a parsing/mapping gap upstream?
6. **[Bangladesh, Brazil, Hong Kong, Indonesia, Japan, Korea, New Zealand, Philippines, Singapore,
   Taiwan, Thailand, Vietnam]** No RSM or L1 control linkage found in any segment across these 12
   tables — does the country simply not have controls/regulatory mappings populated yet, or does
   that linkage live elsewhere for these markets?
7. **[Australia]** 1 of 11 policies has no top-level `policyText` at all. Expected for that specific
   policy type, or a data gap?
8. **[Bangladesh, Brazil, Japan, New Zealand, Philippines, Thailand, Vietnam, Korea]** These markets
   have very small policy populations (2–3 policies each). Is this the true universe of GPPS
   policies for these countries, or is coverage still being onboarded?

